ic edge in a state that still leans Republican.", "watch": "Turnout composition in early voting and whether Paxton consolidates Republican voters after a divisive primary could quickly narrow or flip the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat has become one of the closest races of 2026. With John Cornyn off the ballot after losing renomination, Democrat James Talarico faces scandal-plagued Republican Ken Paxton. Recent polls from mid-October consistently show Talarico narrowly ahead, with averages around 2 to 3 points, though one Republican-sponsored poll had Paxton up one. Talarico has raised a record-shattering $129 million, while outside groups have poured more than $500 million into the race overall, much of it attacking both candidates.\n\nExpert raters are split: most call it a tossup, but Silver Bulletin and Split Ticket rate it Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Talarico's chances around 61-62 percent. The race remains genuinely competitive in a state that normally favors Republicans by six points, so a small but meaningful Democratic edge is the reasonable call heading into early voting.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.65